  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'Place one memory in every row, every column, and every coloured region.


    Two
    memories cannot share a row, a column, or a region. Two memories also cannot
    touch, even diagonally. They may sit on the same diagonal when at least one cell
    is between them.


    Left-click a cell to place a memory. It appears as a white
    glow. Right-click an empty cell to mark it with an X. Right-click that X again
    to remove it.


    A legal memory dims every cell in its row, column, and region,
    plus every cell it touches. Those cells are no longer available.


    If a move
    already breaks a rule, the game explains why and does not spend a heart. If a
    move follows the rules but is not part of the solution, it costs a heart. Undo
    takes a memory back, and the heart comes back with it. Right-click an X again
    to remove it. At zero hearts the puzzle stops. You can undo the last mistake
    or restart.


    A hint explains one forced step. It does not fill the board
    in for you.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
